WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
Dissolve a little bromine in hexane,
and the solution turns orange.

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.730
Keep it in a dark cupboard,
and it stays orange.

3
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:12.790
Stand it in sunlight, and the colour
fades, as hydrogen bromide forms.

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:18.190
Why does bromine in hexane stay orange in
the dark, but lose its colour in sunlight?

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.110
In this mission, you'll meet radicals,

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.110
and the fish-hook arrows that
show single electrons moving.

7
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.350
You'll follow a chain reaction
from initiation to termination,

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.030
and see why alkanes are so unreactive.

9
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.440
Your mission: explain why bromine in
hexane loses its colour only in sunlight.
